== 8. Tirosh malignant vs Belote normal melanocytes ============ 
  CONFOUNDED BY DESIGN: different studies, labs and processing. 
  Shared Smart-seq2 chemistry removes the largest source of 
  difference but not batch, and Belote is counts while Tirosh is 
  log TPM, so only DETECTION can be compared, never level. Depth is 
  matched on detected-gene count using the authors' own n_genes for 
  Belote. Suggestive only. 
  Belote melanocytes: n_genes p10 1647 med 3170 p90 5038 
  Tirosh malignant:   n_genes p10 3544 med 5523 p90 7963 
  common band: 3544-5038 detected genes 

  RASSF9: Belote normal melanocytes 0/2233 = 0.000% [0.000, 0.165] 
     Tirosh malignant melanoma  0/353 = 0.000% [0.000, 1.040] 
     Fisher p = 1.000 (batch-confounded, pseudo-replicated) 

  RASSF10: Belote normal melanocytes 4/2233 = 0.179% [0.049, 0.458] 
     Tirosh malignant melanoma  1/353 = 0.283% [0.007, 1.568] 
     Fisher p = 0.520 (batch-confounded, pseudo-replicated) 

== 9. Verdict against the pre-set criterion ==================== 
  SUPPORTED     = endo+CAF >= 3x malignant in the depth band AND 
                  the donor-level test agrees where available 
  SUGGESTIVE    = ratio holds but donor coverage cannot support a test 
  NOT SUPPORTED = the ratio does not hold 
 
  RASSF9: SUGGESTIVE (no donor-level test available) 
    malignant 0.20% | endo+CAF 19.30% | ratio 95.33x | immune 0.46% 
  RASSF10: NOT SUPPORTED 
    malignant 0.40% | endo+CAF 0.00% | ratio 0.00x | immune 0.00% 
 
  If the immune classes are NOT low, the positive-control logic is 
  unreliable and none of this should be trusted. 

